    "summary": "Cities at the hour when fog takes the streets away and leaves only the tops of things.",
    "story": "<p>I treat cities the way I treat a valley. They have weather, habitats and a daily rhythm, and they're at their strangest before anyone is awake.</p><p>Fog is the great editor. It removes the traffic, the signs and the wires, and gives you back the shape of the place.</p>",
